# cases this column cannot serve: a case name per line, then the reason.

ct/mul_secret  a secret multiply is refused: rv64gc does not select Zkt, which every riscv64 row names. riscv64zkt-linux carries the case.
ct/mul_secret128  same refusal: the secret widening multiply of two 64-bit limbs is a Zkt row. riscv64zkt-linux carries the case.
int128/vector_reinterpret  "scalarize: a bit reinterpret into a vector from a non-vector type is not expanded on a target without SIMD". rv64gc keeps a vector as a memory image, and the scalarize pass does not yet expand a scalar reinterpreted into one; the vector-to-integer direction the case also takes builds. a mach defect, deleted by the change that expands it.
